pg) behaves on Windows, or scope the DC/reap path to POSIX and document the Windows fallback (e.g. plain proc.kill timeout without group reaping).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'subprocess.Popen([pandoc_path, …], start_new_session=True)' and on timeout '`rebar._proc.reap_process_group` … killpg SIGTERM→grace→SIGKILL'","start_new_session maps to os.setsid and killpg are POSIX-only; Windows has neither os.setsid nor os.killpg — a killpg call raises AttributeError/OSError on Windows.","Matrix cell: Platform and venue includes Windows."],"finding":"The renderer builds its own subprocess.Popen with start_new_session=True and reaps via rebar._proc.reap_process_group (killpg-based), both POSIX-only mechanisms; the plan does not state how this behaves on the Windows platform cell of the support matrix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fca57ca69b4fb844e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Hard timeout + process-group reaping + run-level fallback'","norm_id":"nd2d48d65eccf6121","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["Windows workstation/CI running the DC reconcile: a pandoc timeout triggers reap_process_group, which on Windows cannot killpg the process group — the reaper raises or no-ops, orphaning the spinning pandoc grandchild the story exists to kill; the user sees an unreaped process or an exception instead of the intended verbatim fallback."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no"